WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.540
The full trailer for the One Piece live action
series on Netflix if finally here and oh boy

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.940
we do have to talk about it.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:12.019
Within the 3 minutes, we got a closer look
at a ton of stuff, including most of the major

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:17.360
characters, the rough outline of the plot,
the fighting, the cgi and even one major change

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.490
to the main story line.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.970
And I’m just gonna say right out of the
gate, after watching this trailer about 50

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.660
times now: This actual looks pretty damn great.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.730
I am genuinely excited to see the show now,
and I’m blown away that this actually looks

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.760
so promising, after I was a bit torn about
the initial teaser.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.270
BUT!

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:42.230
And yes, of course there was gonna be a but,
there were of course also going to be some

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:47.170
things that really rubbed me the wrong way
and that i want to discuss as well, starting

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:52.210
in order of the trailer with the Execution
of the first pirate king Gol D. Roger.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.240
First of all, this often goes unnoticed in
production, but I really really appreciate

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.949
the sound design of the opening shots.

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:03.540
The sound of the boots and chains, the gears
clanking, the sound of the blade when the

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.360
executioners lift the blade: Great sound design
just elevates the experience so so much and

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.439
makes it so much easier to immerse yourself
into a world.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:18.130
Btw i also love the detail of roger’s jolly
roger on the back of his coat in this shot.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:24.570
The next thing that really really blew me
away here, is the set design of Logue Town:

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:30.270
Holly hell, this looks so so much better than
I could have imagined.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:36.610
Hands down, this might be my favorite set
in the entire show so far next to the Baratie,

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:42.549
although there will be one set I’m personally
very unhappy with, but we’ll get to that.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:48.939
ALSO, and again this is subtle, but has major
impact on how we see a show, is the color

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:54.740
grading here: The washed out yellowy tone
with muted blues gives this exactly the vibe

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:55.939
i was hoping for.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:01.909
It gives the scene such a great ambient feel,
that sells me that this happens in a world

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:04.030
roughly equal to the victorian era.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:07.979
And we also have our first subtle change to
the original anime, because the producers

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:13.580
actually changed the look of the executioners
a little bit, in my opinion very much to the

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.580
better!

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.460
While the two faceless characters here in
the original dont exactly look threatening,

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.390
I really dig the costumes they designed for
the live adaptation.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.530
These guys look like they mean business.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:34.080
AND yet another change that i approve of,
is having Garp be present at Roger’s execution.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.870
This makes sense not only because it introduces
us to Luffy’s grandfather being a high ranking

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.860
marine right from the start, but also because
he was Rogers rival and at some point friend,

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.930
who took in his secret son Ace.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:51.709
AND, it also adds for me to the scene at marineford
where Garp is sitting next to Ace.

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:58.030
If he HAD to be at major executions like this,
it makes it even more painful for Garp having

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:04.879
to be at the execution of two of the people
he really cared for, father and son no less.

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:10.890
OR if he was there voluntarily, it means that
Garp chose to show respect and be there to

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.629
support Roger and Ace.

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:18.299
So, whatever it is, I actually LOVE this change
and kinda wish it had been in the original

00:03:18.299 --> 00:03:19.299
as well.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.799
Also, let’s be real, they absolutely NAILED
Garp here.

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:25.799
Like, you know right away who it was.

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:32.950
Which now brings be to 2 things I didn’t
really like so much, which is the man himself:

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.950
Roger.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.550
Don’t get me wrong, they did absolutely
get the clothing perfect and the voice acting

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.080
is fan-tastic.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.430
BUT.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:47.330
I really don’t vibe with the casting here
for some reason.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:52.599
Nothing against the guy, again i love his
voice performance, but neither the voice nor

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:55.629
his face just scream Roger to me.

00:03:55.629 --> 00:04:01.769
The mustache looks kind of out of place in
his face, and I KNOW there are people who

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:07.239
would have rocked this role, there was actually
a Rumor, that Jack Black was going to play

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:10.370
Roger, which would have been absolutely legendary.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:16.479
I will say, i do love the yellowed teeth,
that is exactly the level of realism, i do

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:18.910
miss a bit from some of the other scenes here.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:23.430
And the second thing I did not really like
here, is the crowd work we see.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:28.090
Now obviously, background acting and crowd
acting is a bit of an ungrateful job sometimes

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.270
and there barely is a lot of camera time on
anyone specific, but the people i they show

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:39.250
here in the crowd, or the woman running with
the sword..maybe I’m being too harsh, but

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:44.270
they don’t really sell to me that these
are real people in a real world.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:49.300
They do feel like someone just screamed action.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.630
But that’s a minor complaint.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:57.280
So moving on to Luffy leaving his home island,
which is called Dawn Island in the manga,

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:02.370
on a tiny boat with no idea how to navigate,
looking out at sea saying he wants to get

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.370
a crew.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:08.180
Now clearly this is what the joke here with
the sea gull is referencing, which by the

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.410
way is called a news coo and is part of the
news paper delivery system in the one piece

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.410
world.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.729
And while it didn’t appear in the original,
i absolutely LOVE how it turned out.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:24.759
I’m actually not 100% sure if this is CGI
or a puppet, but it looks perfectly real to

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:25.759
me.

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:29.819
And I do wonder what type of news it brings
Luffy, that we didn’t get in the manga.

00:05:29.819 --> 00:05:35.680
I assume it might serve as some introduction
or exposition for some characters, though

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:41.020
as far as I know we don’t even know if Luffy
can actually read in the Anime.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.860
Now coming back to the joke itself, this is
something that already was clear during the

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.970
teaser trailer, but we’re clearly going
to get a lot of these very Marvel-like one

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:56.810
liners, that I personally just don’t find
super funny, but I can live with them, and

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:57.810
it is what it is.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:03.400
Also in this case it even works somewhat,
because Luffy would probably be the type of

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:08.120
person who would have invited a sea gull into
his crew in the manga, if it had landed on

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.430
his boat at this point.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.740
Also, I’m not gonna play any music for copyright
reasons, but that track that starts playing

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:19.259
right after, that sounds like a bit of a rip
off of the pirates of the Caribbean theme

00:06:19.259 --> 00:06:20.259
right?

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:21.259
I’m not imagining that?

00:06:21.259 --> 00:06:22.340
Okay good.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.720
Weird choice, I’d rather would have preferred
a more visual nod to that series by making

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.220
things look less clean and more ‘real’,
but hey.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:34.970
We get the iconic Luffy in a barrel scene,
however he managed to get in there, which

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:39.300
I’m really looking forward to seeing him
explode out of there in front of Koby.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:44.880
Which brings us right to Alivida’s ship,
which is in the process of plundering another

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.880
pirate ship.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:46.880
AND.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.960
I. LOVE IT: The fact that they actually show
a somewhat realistic pirate battle with people

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.740
swinging on ropes and canons being fired,
is something that is even missing a bit from

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:02.340
the original show, so to me this really helps
sell me this world, especially considering

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.150
that we are still in the east blue here, where
things like Devil Fruits and Haki are insanely

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.380
rare and most people don’t even know they
exist.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:16.350
I think Alvida’s ship design is really awesome,
actually better than the going merry in my

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:23.129
opinion, where the sheep’s head still haunts
my dreams.

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:25.590
Alvida herself is..alright I guess.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:31.050
The casting and costume is great, but she
almost doesn’t look mean enough here, if

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.050
you know what i mean.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.100
Thought that might end up being just fine
in the final series.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:42.129
ALSO, for SOME REASON, here the pirate ships
look dirty, edgy and Real.

00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:46.810
Just what I was hoping for, but then so many
other sets, like the Merry or the cosumes

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:52.039
of so many characters are so so clean.

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:54.330
look at those dirty sails with holes in them.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.980
Now THAT’s what i would have loved for everything
in this show.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:02.500
Now I’ll be honest, I’m not really sure
what the red explosion here is, but it does

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.350
look visually stunning, so I’m excited to
see that in the show.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:09.949
And then: The Jolly Roger reveal!!

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:15.470
And even though there is some somewhat corny
dialogue here again, I couldnt help but grin

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:21.270
seeing this: They took the exact design from
the manga, which I really really appreciate

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:25.300
and actually I do really buy the acting for
Luffy here too.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:30.210
Small fun fact, the first person in the manga
to every say the phrase straw hat pirates

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:38.080
is actually not Luffy, but the Marine Captain
Smoker during the Alabasta arc.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:45.399
Then we get a bit of a traveling montage,
which sets up the goal of reaching the grandline,

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:50.450
which i strongly assume will be the conclusion
of this first season: Reaching Reverse Mountain.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:54.950
Because Entering the Grand Line and Meeting
Laboon would in my opinion make the perfect

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:59.820
first episode of a second season, kicking
of the Alabasta Saga.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:06.750
Im not sure why the merry is capsizing here
in this shot, but it does look awesome as

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.750
heck.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:13.380
Then we get a first look at buggy’s circus
tent, which I also think turned out awesome.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:18.860
In fact, Buggy, his crew and the set make
them seem way more of a threat than their

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.920
original appearance in the manga.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.060
Ah…and then Mihawk.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.060
So.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:29.330
Mihawk himself is as perfect as I could have
ever dreamed it.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:35.029
Steven Ward is just perfect in this role,
the costume is flawless and even the colored

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:38.400
contacts work perfectly here.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:42.089
The fight scene with Zoro at the Baratie is
bound to be one of the biggest highlights

00:09:42.089 --> 00:09:43.089
of the show.

00:09:43.089 --> 00:09:48.830
And yet: WHY ..why does the sword look it’s
made out of plastic.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:55.329
Yoru in this closeup looks like some low budget
merchandize and that’s such a shame.

00:09:55.329 --> 00:10:02.209
Yes, making big anime weapons look real is
hard, but there are whole youtube channels

00:10:02.209 --> 00:10:04.770
out there doing just that.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:10.260
For comparison, look at the version of Yoru
that the craft channel AWE me made 8 years

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.260
ago.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:16.829
Then we have the scene with Captain Kuro’s
Claws appearing behind Merry, Kaya’s butler

00:10:16.829 --> 00:10:18.170
from Usopps home island.

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:21.710
And yes he’s actually called merry, because
he’s the one who built the original Going

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:27.450
Merry.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:32.000
Fantastic little teaser for this arc here
and Kuro will be a super fun villain to see

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.910
in Live Action as well with his massive claw
hands, that we actually see a bit later again

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.210
boring into the floor next to luffy.

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:43.420
Then there is Zoro in a well for some reason.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.420
And ahhh.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.420
Yes.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.529
So, this trailer sadly confirmed something
I was a bit worried about with the teaser

00:10:49.529 --> 00:10:54.779
and this might be a very controversial take,
but here it is: I’m just not buying Zoro

00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:55.779
as a character.

00:10:55.779 --> 00:11:01.720
Don’t get me wrong, Makenyu LOOKS like the
perfect Zoro, the fight scenes LOOK perfectly

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:07.030
like Zoro, but the dialogue and the way he
talks…sorry but that’s just not Zoro.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:14.040
Yes, Zoro is supposed to be cool, but what
makes him so unique is also his comedic moments,

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:19.500
when he lets that cool facade slip and how
much he really cares about the entire crew.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:24.690
And I’m really sorry, but to me, that’s
just not what I’m seeing here.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:29.320
Which is just such a shame, because he one
of my absolute favorite characters in the

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.320
show.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:35.730
We also get Zoro’s oath to Luffy, which
is also quite altered from the manga.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:41.050
There it happens with Zoro’s chest cut open
after losing to Mihawk and almost drowning

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:46.970
balling his eyes out, which is one of the
few emotional moments that make Zoro so awesome.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:51.610
And i might be wrong and we still get that
scene as it happens, but if this turns out

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:56.269
to be the actual oath scene, than im just
not buying it.

00:11:56.269 --> 00:12:03.090
But moving on to something that looks just
incredible, we have Buggy and his powers,

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.670
and they look AWESOME.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:13.120
The CGI for his powers absolutely work, the
set as i mentioned is epic and this will absolutely

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:20.620
go down as a highlight of this first season.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:27.120
Which now brings us to what is clearly going
to be the climax of this show: The fight against

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:32.660
the fishman pirates, which interestingly enough
seems to be set up at the Baratie.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:38.360
This will of course be probably THE single
biggest change to the original, because it

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:44.329
seems like Don Krieg, the main villain of
that arc has been replaced by Arlong and his

00:12:44.329 --> 00:12:49.630
men, who might be there to take back Nami
by force, instead of Nami betraying the crew.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:55.399
And while this might end up being a controversial
choice, it might work out in their favor,

00:12:55.399 --> 00:12:59.120
as long as they make sure we get these 3 things:

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:05.240
First, Mihawk still needs his epic entrance,
and I doubt that he will sink Arlong’s ship.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:09.970
Then, we still need to see Sanji’s kindness,
which was him giving food to the starving

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.329
Gin in the manga.

00:13:12.329 --> 00:13:18.470
And thirdly, Nami not ‘betraying’/leaving
the crew on her own accords would be quite

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:22.870
a drastic change to her character arc and
her redemption later on in the story when

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:26.620
she fully trusts luffy to save her and her
village.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:31.630
But that being said, if they manage to work
these things in, I don’t hate the idea of

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:36.060
setting up the Fishmen as the final villains
of this season a bit earlier.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:45.380
Also, and I can’t stress this enough: The
Baratie set is by far the most epic thing

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:49.480
in this entire trailer for me.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:55.980
It just looks so damn fantastic, that it’s
obvious that they really went above and beyond

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.160
to design this, and I’m all here for it.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.100
Which sadly I can’t say about Arlong Park
as well.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:09.250
Because this just looks like Disney land,
fake plastic rocks to me, im sorry.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:16.440
The main building itself looks great, both
on the inside and on the outside and when

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:19.860
we see it collapse, that looks very real to
me too.

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:24.589
But the yard in front of it, again i just
don’t buy.

00:14:24.589 --> 00:14:27.449
It’s like Mihawks sword.

00:14:27.449 --> 00:14:34.149
however, what does look very very promising
is the fighting choreography.

00:14:34.149 --> 00:14:37.329
All the non-cgi characters powers look incredible.

00:14:37.329 --> 00:14:40.350
Zoro’s sword skills, Sanji’s kicks, Usopp’s
sniping.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:42.150
They are all fantastic.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:50.339
And I’m glad to see that there will be blood
in this show as well, as we see Zoro ruthlessly

00:14:50.339 --> 00:14:51.860
slashing someones heel.

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:56.750
This makes me very confident that the actual
fight scenes might end up being a real joy

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.750
to watch.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.360
Luffy’s CGI that we see, him stretching
his face, just like in the Mange and then

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:08.610
his gatling gun are actually as perfect as
you could have made it for a power that feels

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:13.329
almost impossible to bring to live in a live
action setting.

00:15:13.329 --> 00:15:15.149
Hats off to the show runners for this.

00:15:15.149 --> 00:15:16.889
I 100% buy it.

00:15:16.889 --> 00:15:21.950
Arlong himself on the other hand.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:22.950
Ouch.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:27.769
I mean same thing here: It was always going
to be very very hard to bring the fishman

00:15:27.769 --> 00:15:31.709
to live properly, but this just doesn’t
look quite right to me.

00:15:31.709 --> 00:15:40.380
I wonder if dropping the long nose, like they
did with usopp might not have been the wiser

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.509
move here.

00:15:41.509 --> 00:15:47.370
The scene of Luffy giving Nami his straw hat,
which next to Zoro’s oath is probably the

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:53.180
best scene in the entire east blue saga in
the manga, could really go either way here.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:16:00.360
I didn’t quite feel the heaviness of the
scene here, but it is just a quick snippet

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:05.720
from a trailer with upbeat epic music, so
it might end up being just fine in the show

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:08.670
with more context.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:13.480
Both Shanks AND the sea King look absolutely
awesome.

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:18.880
Very excited to see how Shanks’ lines and
delivery will be like, but this looks great.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:24.290
As does the iconinc giving luffy his straw
hat scene, though i think the background farming

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:29.180
could have been a bit cleaner, maybe with
the ocean.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:33.269
We see Morgan and his axe hand, again very
promising.

00:16:33.269 --> 00:16:36.060
And boy, Koby is just Koby.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.470
That is as perfect as it gets.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.790
Dialogue, costume, everything.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:46.339
And we do get 3 little easter eggs in the
bounty posters luffy looks at, all from pirates

00:16:46.339 --> 00:16:50.980
Luffy will meet in the grandline with Bellamy
from Skypea, Foxy who set up the davy back

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.529
fight and cavendish who joined Luffy’s grand
fleet on Dressrosa.

00:16:54.529 --> 00:17:00.069
I hope these are little hints, that we might
be seeing these people in later seasons.

00:17:00.069 --> 00:17:08.230
Buuuut, I don’t really did the delivery
of the king of the pirates line at the end.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:13.569
That’s not really Luffy for me, but that
might be my personal taste here.

00:17:13.569 --> 00:17:19.709
However, while I do have a couple of issues
like this one, overall this live action might

00:17:19.709 --> 00:17:24.420
actually turn out to not only be better than
we all expected, but I’d actually go so

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:27.600
far as to say that this trailer was really
really good.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:33.130
If the show itself can live up to what we
are being shown here, then I think new and

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:37.630
old fans, me included, will have a fantastic
time watching it, so make sure to subscribe

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:41.510
if you don’t want to miss my breakdown of
everything once the show actually drops on

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:42.910
August 31st.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.429
Thanks for watching.

